# scenario 06.8: check-design checks each note that a pull request changes
# main holds a correct note of 07. The branch notes changes that note, which
# stays correct, and adds a note of 08 without the section Goal: only the
# note of 08 is rejected. The branch readme changes no note and passes.
env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Agent GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=agent@example.com GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Agent GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=agent@example.com
cd repo
exec git init -q -b main
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m base

exec git checkout -q -b notes main
cp ../note-07 docs/increments/07-sample/design.md
mkdir docs/increments/08-later
cp ../note-08 docs/increments/08-later/design.md
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m notes
exitcode 1 factory check-design --base main
stdout '^check-design: error \S*docs/increments/08-later/design\.md(:\d+)?: missing-section( |$)'
! stdout 'error \S*07-sample'
stdout '^check-design: \d+ errors$'

exec git checkout -q -b readme main
cp ../readme README.md
exec git commit -q -a -m readme
exec factory check-design --base main
stdout '^check-design: ok 0 checked$'
! stdout ': error '

-- readme --
# Sample, changed
-- note-07 --
# Increment 07: sample

## Goal

- The sample tool of increment 07 works.
- It also works for a second kind of thing.

## Out of scope

- Everything else.

## Existing tools

- None found; searched for sample tools.

## Interface

- `sample run`

## Rollout

- Off switch: none. Failure signal: the tool rejects a correct input.

## Evidence

- Approved scenarios: 07.1.

## Scenarios

- **scenario 07.1** (automated) **A sample thing works.** Given a sample thing, the tool accepts it.
